{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark","id":851878,"title":"A World not so Dark","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-23T11:08:32-07:00","id":851878,"title":"A World not so Dark","content":"Does anyone else have any recommendations for how to run a less heavy WOD game. I love the deep narrative and adaptable mechanics that pretty much allow you to do anything(Even from other franchises, I've run more than one technocracy games modeled after SCPs and xcom), but the &quot;True art is angsty&quot; and &quot;the man is keeping us down&quot; tropes it relies on heavily in straight WOD make me think of bad fanfiction sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any tweaks, story and mechanics wise, that can mend this somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T12:43:06-07:00","id":851936,"title":"","content":"Remember that all monsters have lives. Sometimes you just gotta go eat a hotdog.<br /> <br /> A lot can be done by just playing to the slice of life mentality, creating tangled knots that don't need cutting, using setting problems instead of character problems, talking to players and establishing the tone and direction.<br /> <br /> THe single most epic Mage game I ever played spent it's first half more or less following the lives this little drug-dealing cabal. We did stuff like invade a Mormon temple, go to a recovering drug addict's party, hosted a small mage convention at the club, find a way to send a whiny little brother back to Portland, stuff like that. Even our encounters with other drug crews often ended up as &quot;Run the Fuck away&quot; or &quot;Hey, instead of shooting each other in the head, you wanna talk things out like reasonable adults?&quot; It was good fun, idle days with things going on, but nothing too heavy. All this without actually hacking the setting or mechanics<br /> <br /> The second half turned into the usual emotional torture fest/stop the world from ending thing you might expect from WoD, and it was more potent because of the first half.<br /> <br /> So, really, it's largely in how you run the game. Sometimes, you just gotta go eat a hotdog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T02:18:12-07:00","id":852295,"title":"","content":"Why not to use a fictional world like a teslapunk version of Scarred lands or Ravenloft settings?<br /> <br /> Really it is very easy, you only need to change some things from the canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T03:26:15-07:00","id":852309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark#post851878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else have any recommendations for how to run a less heavy WOD game. I love the deep narrative and adaptable mechanics that pretty much allow you to do anything(Even from other franchises, I've run more than one technocracy games modeled after SCPs and xcom), but the &quot;True art is angsty&quot; and &quot;the man is keeping us down&quot; tropes it relies on heavily in straight WOD make me think of bad fanfiction sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any tweaks, story and mechanics wise, that can mend this somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need to tweak anything in the mechanics. Just change the tone of your stories. Focus on the good things, give the characters a victory or two. Do not make everyone they work with out to get them. Give them genuine friends and positive changes, and the world will look different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:10:51-07:00","id":852589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=852309#post852309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You don't need to tweak anything in the mechanics. Just change the tone of your stories. Focus on the good things, give the characters a victory or two. Do not make everyone they work with out to get them. Give them genuine friends and positive changes, and the world will look different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exaxctly. Even Vampire can take on a completely different aspect. Can vitae arrest congenital conditions? Can you keep your brother from dying from leukemia? Or make it so your grandmother's crippling arthritis goes into remission and she can dance again? That's not exactly light-hearted, but it's not dark. How about a vampire that's trying to still be a good father to his kids and husband to his wife. Sure, she's effectively his blood doll, but, not really. How do you keep up the &quot;Masquerade&quot; if you have to keep 8 year olds from wanting to bring their dad to show and tell &quot;cause he's a vampire&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's the hardest sell. Mage can be so NOT dark so very very easily. <br /> <br /> Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T15:04:37-07:00","id":852626,"title":"","content":"I think the hardest part about making vampire less dark is the need for blood. You can't really make drinking blood not dark without making it silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T16:05:21-07:00","id":852644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=852626#post852626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the hardest part about making vampire less dark is the need for blood. You can't really make drinking blood not dark without making it silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, that little matter of the Kiss and its unfortunate implications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T18:27:56-07:00","id":852719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=852626#post852626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the hardest part about making vampire less dark is the need for blood. You can't really make drinking blood not dark without making it silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's very little about Vampire that can be seen in a positive light. But if you really want to, just downplay the kiss, the Hunt and the blood. Play Vampions and kill some Baali and Methusalehs and terrorists. There.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T21:21:43-07:00","id":853320,"title":"","content":"My WoD games cling far more to a 2nd Edition feel than anything else.<br /> The world is definitely 'dark' but has never been as completely and utterly hopeless as Revised painted it to be.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can have friends, those that you can trust your life with and you aren't worried about sticking a knife between your ribs as soon as you turn your back.<br /> It's still morally abhorrent to suck the life blood from a mortal, but taking just enough from a would-be lover whilst wrapped in shadow in the corner of a busy nightclub, then leaving them with memories of a passion-filled night plays more into the gothic imagery than the out-and-out horror dynamic.<br /> <br /> There's nothing pretty about my WoD but I've always refused to indulge in some of the nihilism Revised edition paints the setting with.<br /> <br /> I've played in games where every NPC answers you with a curt reply and snidey smirk, where the world and his wife is out to screw you over and almost everything your character does is met with failure and loss.<br /> It gets tiring very, very quickly.<br /> Games are meant to be fun. If you come away from your session feeling frustrated or depressed there is something wrong going on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T11:25:27-07:00","id":853587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andreas Rayne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=853320#post853320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My WoD games cling far more to a 2nd Edition feel than anything else.<br /> The world is definitely 'dark' but has never been as completely and utterly hopeless as Revised painted it to be.<br /> <br /> Yes, you can have friends, those that you can trust your life with and you aren't worried about sticking a knife between your ribs as soon as you turn your back.<br /> It's still morally abhorrent to suck the life blood from a mortal, but taking just enough from a would-be lover whilst wrapped in shadow in the corner of a busy nightclub, then leaving them with memories of a passion-filled night plays more into the gothic imagery than the out-and-out horror dynamic.<br /> <br /> There's nothing pretty about my WoD but I've always refused to indulge in some of the nihilism Revised edition paints the setting with.<br /> <br /> I've played in games where every NPC answers you with a curt reply and snidey smirk, where the world and his wife is out to screw you over and almost everything your character does is met with failure and loss.<br /> It gets tiring very, very quickly.<br /> Games are meant to be fun. If you come away from your session feeling frustrated or depressed there is something wrong going on.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. I hated the Call of Cthuluh-esk &quot;Your hope isn't that you win, but instead that you are too small for the enemy to notice you&quot; plot revised was trying to turn the game into. It railroads the story and takes the ability to make meaningful decisions from the players and storyteller alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T04:17:44-07:00","id":853968,"title":"","content":"When I played and ran chronicles I found the best games to be mixed with good and bad, too much of one without enough of the other can make the game frustrating and dull. <br /> <br /> Ask your players what kinda game they want, find the things large and small that they like and want and put it in. Add more with your ideas and slight twists to their requests. <br /> <br /> A good example is before I started being a ST. The ST at the time wanted a stark contrast, light and dark. So another player and I did a most unlikely romance in the backdrop of a Four Horsemen apocolapyse. So ontop of the usual intrigue, we had her Tremere ex-Archon and my Caitiff elder Scourge (told ya ) meet and and become paramours as they were feared and excluded by most of the other Licks. They also were the focal characters fighting to prevent the doom, as others worried about their own unlives, ours simply didn't want to lose the one good thing in their lives. <br /> <br /> Paramour is also a merit, I learned. Nice to know that even the Kindred can try to kindle flames. <br /> <br /> In the end he broke many a rule and by the luck of the dice he succeeded . And I'm talking the stuff of legends, I think he really wanted us to fail. They saved the day...then the Prince tried to exile him. The twists and turns continued but we always had something to work for, to keep that light burning bright in a dark world. <br /> <br /> Ultimately we changed the tone of the game by doing a unusual romance. Others seeing our enjoyment of this new dynamic started adding their own personal twists and on the whole the game added a deep personal involvement within the wider Chronicle storylines. <br /> <br /> When I took over I did player run scenes where they submitted ideas they had and I would let them run them on their own. I'd play as a character and assist if they needed help. I also ran some unreal scenes that belonged in a action or thriller movie just to spice things up. <br /> <br /> It is a World of Darkness but darkness is darkest when a light burns bright within it. I hope this helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am also known as Kevlar...shoulda made that my user name. &gt;.&gt;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2366-lasombra077","name":"Lasombra077","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:44:46-07:00","id":854156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=852589#post852589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How about a vampire that's trying to still be a good father to his kids and husband to his wife. Sure, she's effectively his blood doll, but, not really. How do you keep up the &quot;Masquerade&quot; if you have to keep 8 year olds from wanting to bring their dad to show and tell &quot;cause he's a vampire&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's the hardest sell. Mage can be so NOT dark so very very easily.<br /> <br /> Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of the Vampire Dad template in &quot;Time of Thin Blood&quot;. One thing that could help with VTM is playing with the pre-revised concept of Golconda being not only achievable, but a more permenant state. Or that there are Vampires that can achieve and maintain a high humanity and/or become better people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T12:52:41-07:00","id":854163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/851878-a-world-not-so-dark?p=854156#post854156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reminds me of the Vampire Dad template in &quot;Time of Thin Blood&quot;. One thing that could help with VTM is playing with the pre-revised concept of Golconda being not only achievable, but a more permenant state. Or that there are Vampires that can achieve and maintain a high humanity and/or become better people.</div> </div> </div> </div>A long time ago, I ran an elder's game where one of the characters worked really really hard to achieve and maintain a Humanity 10. It was glorious. And very very tricky. Particularly since the rest of the coterie were not at all like that and were weirded out by the whole thing. (Oh, and the whole &quot;How do you feed without provoking a Humanity check?&quot; thing. She was pretty good at coming up with very saintly ways of getting blood...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T06:47:53-07:00","id":866368,"title":"","content":"? I don't really see a challenge in running a non-dark WoD game with the rules as-is. Althugh the WooD/CoD books like to remind you that this is a SERIOUS game with SERIOUS psychological exploration etc. in the TEXT every chance they get, the RULES rarely actually grow up to this promise. It is very easy to end up with a &quot;dark superheroes&quot; game even unintentionally if the GM does not make that extra effort to add the angsty content him/herself.<br /> <br /> Obviously, you could try to remove all the &quot;you're screwed either way&quot; mkechanics if you wanted it to make super light. Golconda? Why, half our vampires have achieved that, it's not that hard! Frenzy? Nah, it doesn't trigger when yiou don't want it anymore. Masquerade? Actually, we have pretty good relationship with some humans. Conspiracies? Most of our factions actually get along quite well, and we even run self-help groups for those who have difficulties with fitting in. etcetra.<br /> But yeah in that case you're probably better off with another game where these are already the intended setting, to save yourself the work of reimagininghow thing'd work yourself<br /> (I mean, I could rewrite it because I'm awesome, but I imagine you'd rather have help with the setting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2330-vree","name":"Vree","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T07:01:23-07:00","id":866371,"title":"","content":"One thing I always do is that in my games, when a vampire achieves Golconda (and it's actually achievable in my games), they become human again. End of story. 1e sort of implied this without directly spelling it out, but it quickly fell by the wayside past the 1e corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}